mkdir
Usage: mkdir [-m MODE] [-p] DIRECTORY...

Create DIRECTORY.

	-m MODE	Permissions at creation, octal (700) or symbolic (u=rwx)
	-p	No error if exists; make parent directories as needed

Setting the mode at creation rather than with a later `chmod` means the
directory is never briefly readable by anyone it should not be. ``700`` is
yours alone; see `chmod` for the arithmetic.
